A||||7||Bruce||Speaker screen help||||1||
Z||000000||Bruce||08-10-2000||08:39 PM||||I'm going to replace the fabric that's used on the dashboard speaker screens. What's the best way to remove the grills without harming the dashboard?<BR>Thanks!<BR>bb||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||08-10-2000||09:30 PM||||gently pry them up on both sides with a flat blade screwdriver.......<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/WHGD_sig.gif">                <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||08-10-2000||09:31 PM||||The grills are held by four plastic pins in each corner. I find it easiest without any damage to pry them out with a putty knife. Just work it out a little at a time at each side. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||1
